# lit-k (M6): k's meaning on the plane while k is the active value (FV 04: the pointer on k's
# row). R3 as in `transformed` (a 2, h −1, k 1 and P's 0.5 typed into their fields on both: M8 made
# P's a field in the port), in Arctic Ice; then the pointer onto k's
# row (its name at (200, 468); the row is (49, 446.5, 394 x 44) in the reference's DOM): k's
# dimension line, 2.5 px of --primary from y = 0 up to y = k at x = h, (−1, 0) to (−1, 1), with
# its 9 px start tick and its arrowhead, under the curve; k's row and term lit in the sidebar. Each
# click waits a frame before the typing, as text input starts when the box's field opens.
size 1440 900
density 2
scheme dark
mode dark
theme arctic-ice
wait 300
click 383 424
wait 16
type "2"
key Enter
click 383 468
wait 16
type "1"
key Enter
click 383 573
wait 16
type "-1"
key Enter
click 330 690
wait 16
type "0.5"
key Enter
click 760 48
wait 2000
move 200 468
wait 500
shot lit-k
